WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.490
With the fourth and final season of The Good
Place fast approaching, fans are excited to

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.960
see what happens to Jason, Tahani, Chidi,
and Eleanor as they attempt to get into the

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.259
real Good Place.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.240
Well, here's what we know about the upcoming
season so far.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:14.480
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.940
The Good Place might seem like a typical network
comedy, but it shirks convention in several

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.000
important ways.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.080
For one thing, all of its main characters
are dead.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.460
Except for a brief time when they weren't.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.560
Forgive us for stating the obvious.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.300
"Ya basic!"

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.060
Thanks to its penchant for philosophy, complex
plot points, and strong performances, the

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:39.410
series also brings a distinct sense of "prestige
TV" to a network comedy.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.980
Well, maybe not all the time.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.860
"This place truly is paradise."

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.340
Also, a typical season of The Good Place runs
much shorter than your average TV show.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:54.130
There are fewer than 15 episodes per season,
whereas most sitcoms feature 22 to 24 episodes

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:54.800
per season.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.520
Here's some good news for you: The final season
of The Good Place will reportedly consist

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.160
of fourteen episodes, making it the longest
season in the show's history.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.600
What's more, series creator Mike Schur has
announced that the finale will run for a full

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.100
hour.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.780
As great as that is, it still signals the
end of a beloved show.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.500
"Really sucks."

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:18.060
In June 2019, Schur took to Twitter to announce
the show was ending, writing:

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.840
"At times over the past few years we've been
tempted to go beyond four seasons, but mostly

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:26.240
because making this show is a rare, creatively
fulfilling joy."

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.820
That's right: The decision to end the show
came from the creative team rather than NBC

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:31.320
brass.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.520
As Schur tweeted,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.990
"Given the ideas we wanted to explore, and
the pace at which we wanted to present those

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:42.520
ideas, I began to feel like four seasons - just
over 50 episodes - was the right lifespan."

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:43.960
"I'm not mad.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.420
I'm just disappointed."

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.549
On the upside, at least the talented folks
behind The Good Place get to end the show

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:51.540
on their own terms.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.020
If you need a quick brushup seasons past,
you've come to the right place.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.920
The Good Place covers a lot of ground from
episode so episode, and it's a truly unpredictable

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.420
show.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.600
If you don't believe us, just look at all
these magical shrimp from the first episode.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:10.319
The show gets off to a running start by introducing
us to Eleanor Shellstrop, portrayed by Kristen

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:10.820
Bell.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.500
And what a way to do it.

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:17.040
Shortly after she meets Michael - played by
Ted Danson - she's informed that she's full-on

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.400
dead and has been granted a spot in the "Good
Place" instead of the "Bad Place."

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:22.320
"Cool.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.000
Cool.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.099
I have some questions."

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:26.600
"I thought you might."

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.380
Here's another twist - the first of many.

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:34.220
Eleanor was a total dirtbag during her time
on Earth, and she doesn't actually belong

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.220
in the Good Place.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:40.040
If you haven't seen the show, run away right
now - because, spoiler alert: Eleanor isn't

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.360
even in the Good Place.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.800
"Oh, man!"

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.060
It's true.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:55.060
At the end of the first season, Eleanor and
her cohorts find out they're actually in a

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.080
"Bad Place" that was specifically designed
to torture them.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.460
Eventually, the humans team up with Michael
to work against the many demons of the "Bad

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:02.960
Place."

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.480
Upon discovering that nobody has actually
been admitted to the "Good Place" in recent

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.640
memory, the gang decides to reboot their memories
with Michael's help.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.780
That way, they can work on improving themselves
in the afterlife.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.800
It's a last ditch attempt to earn spots in
the real "Good Place."'

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:18.300
Confused?

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.480
Get used to it.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.380
"Ya know what, Michael?

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.800
Ya ba…"

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.620
Eleanor starts to suspect she's been put in
The Good Place by mistake, and subsequently

00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:29.859
embarks on a mission to become a better person.

00:03:29.859 --> 00:03:34.890
And she's in luck, because one of her companions
is Chidi, a professor of ethics and moral

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:35.500
philosophy.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.860
Once she explains her dilemma, he reluctantly
agrees to teach her how to become a better

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.360
person.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.940
"I'm getting a stomach ache.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.760
I'm in a perfect utopia and, yeah, I have
a stomachache."

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.980
There's a whole lot of philosophy in The Good
Place, a show that references everyone from

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.480
Kant to Kierkegaard... yet it somehow remains
utterly hilarious while doing so.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.140
As The New York Times notes:

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:00.720
"The most refreshing thing about The Good
Place, in an era of artistic bleakness, is

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.700
its optimism about human nature.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.620
It's made humane and sidesplittingly entertaining
television out of the notion that people - and

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.500
even the occasional immortal demon - are redeemable."

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.999
Thanks to its endlessly inventive and hilarious
premise, The Good Place earned excellent reviews

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:16.900
right out of the gate.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.360
And that sinister-yet-silly twist at the end
of the first season really made people pay

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:21.860
attention.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.460
Pulitzer Prize winning critic Emily Nussbaum
wrote:

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.860
"What we got was the rare season finale that
could legitimately be described as a game-changer,

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:35.570
vaulting the show from a daffy screwball comedy
to something darker, much stranger, and uncomfortably

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:38.020
appropriate for our apocalyptic era."

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:43.000
Speaking of high praise: In 2019, Kristen
Bell was nominated for a Golden Globe for

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.930
"Best Performance by an Actress in a Television
Series: Musical or Comedy."

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:51.920
But alas, she ultimately lost to Rachel Brosnahan,
the star of The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.120
"Oh, you gotta be forkin' kidding me."

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.760
Nevertheless, The Good Place won a prestigious
Peabody Award in April 2019, and it secured

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:05.500
its first-ever nomination for "Outstanding
Comedy Series" at the 2019 Emmys.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.260
On the whole, that's none too shabby.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:12.200
After Mike Schur's success with The Office
and Parks and Recreation, it's not surprising

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.260
that NBC wanted to work with him again.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:18.400
When he pitched the show that eventually became
The Good Place, the network was instantly

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.480
sold on the idea.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:25.430
In fact, NBC execs committed to a 13-episode
season before a single episode had been produced.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.580
Prior to its premiere in 2016, the show was
shrouded in secrecy - but Schur did make it

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:34.260
known that he loosely modeled the show on
ABC's massive hit Lost.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:39.190
In fact, Damon Lindelof - the executive producer
of Lost and The Leftovers - worked with Schur

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.760
to come up with The Good Place's central concept.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.400
Schur's wanted to create a show that tied
together philosophy, religion, comedy, and

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.100
the afterlife.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.680
It's a lot to wrap one's head around, isn't
it?

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:55.040
"I'm sorry - I'm trying to process a tremendous
amount of insane information."

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.420
Nevertheless, Schur succeeded in creating
one of the most unique shows to ever air on

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.420
network TV.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:05.180
So: at the end of season one, we learn that
the "Good Place" is an experiment created

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.980
by Michael to torment the poor souls who wound
up there.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.430
"You thought we would torture each other…
and we did, for a little.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.520
But we also took care of each other."

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:19.400
It sounds like the final season will continue
to explore this conceit, with some fresh faces

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.480
thrown into the mix.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.390
Mike Schur told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.900
"They're going to repeat this grand experiment
[…] and see what happens when it's new people.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:31.680
Their wager is that any group of people, if
given a certain amount of love, support, empathy

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:33.140
and help, can become better.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.120
That essentially no one is beyond rehabilitation."

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:40.800
Meanwhile, William Jackson Harper - the actor
who plays Chidi - told TV Insider:

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.560
"We're starting in a very different place
where the six of us are not all on the same

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.940
page at all […] So, it leads to some really
interesting dynamics.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.340
And I think it'll be a really interesting
watch.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.000
But that's about all I can say."

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:57.080
The Good Place doesn't have a huge cast, but
two notable names have been attached to the

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.760
show from the beginning: Kristen Bell and
Ted Danson.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:04.840
Danson of course, is a comedy legend, best
known for his work as Sam Malone on Cheers.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:09.680
Since his sitcom heyday, he's appeared in
shows like Bored to Death, CSI, and Curb Your

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:10.690
Enthusiasm.

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:15.250
As for Bell, she played the titular teenage
detective on Veronica Mars and then went on

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:19.590
to appear in films including Forgetting Sarah
Marshall, The Boss, and Couples Retreat, to

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:20.380
name just a few.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:25.000
Of course, Bell has since reprised her role
as Veronica Mars in both a feature film and

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.900
a Hulu revival of the series.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:31.080
It's not a stretch to say that The Good Place
boasts one of the most talented casts on network

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.080
television - and several of them were relatively
unknowns when the series began.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:39.740
William Jackson Harper was cast early on,
followed by British television presenter Jameela

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:41.660
Jamil in her first acting role.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.240
Then there's Manny Jacinto, another newcomer.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:49.080
The final piece of the puzzle is D'Arcy Carden,
the brilliant comedic actress who plays the

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:49.580
role of Janet.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.160
She's sort of like the afterlife's answer
to Siri.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:56.620
"I mean, it does matter if I know things because
I'm an informational delivery system... and

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.480
I don't have a heart, but thanks!"

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.980
Over the course of three seasons, The Good
Place has continued to expand its supporting

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:03.480
cast.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:08.320
Notable additions include Marc Evan Jackson,
who plays a Bad Place bureaucrat named Shawn.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.350
Then there's Saturday Night Live standout
Maya Rudolph, who plays an all-powerful and

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.200
exceptionally batty judge.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:18.940
That's to say nothing of Kirby Howell-Baptiste,
the British actress who plays Simone.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:23.600
She's a neuroscientist who strikes up a relationship
with Chidi when the group finds themselves

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.620
back on Earth.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:29.700
"What we do is, we make a lengthy incision
from your eyebrow to the nape of your neck,

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.780
and we peel your face back, all right?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.280
And slice your skull open..."

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:37.920
According to Schur, there will be some exciting
new additions to the cast in season four.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:42.320
In an interview with TVLine, he said that
the final season will focus on a full reboot

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.520
of the main gang's memories in the afterlife.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:48.320
Each of them will be confronted by someone
who was specifically engineered to torture

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:48.820
them.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.320
Tahani and Chidi's torturers were revealed
in the third season, but Eleanor and Jason's

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.320
worst nightmares are still unknown to us - and
them.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:57.420
As Schur puts it,

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:01.680
"The idea was that the Bad Place chose the
people they chose to specifically kind of

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.430
smart-bomb our original crew.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.920
[...] They’re just people whose personalities
[...] are specifically designed to ruin the

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.870
lives of one individual [...]. So we really
spent a lot of time trying to figure out what

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.760
that would mean for the final two residents."

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.620
Schur didn't reveal any specifics beyond that,
but bringing these tormentors to life will

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:21.840
almost certainly add some memorable players
to an already excellent cast.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:26.320
Clearly The Good Place has made a name for
itself as one of the most life-affirming shows

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:30.190
on television - no small feat for a show about
a bunch of dead people.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:33.800
Well, it sounds like the final season is going
to pack an emotional punch.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:39.070
The creative team is keeping major plot details
under wraps, but actor Manny Jacinto did hint

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:41.800
at a touching final season, telling E! Online:

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.700
"I think It'll really hit the heartstrings.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.180
I mean last season's finale was definitely
kind of hitting people in the feels, but I

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:51.530
think this season, we've kind of headed in
that kind of sort of direction."

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:55.870
Meanwhile, Mike Schur has promised not to
end the final season on a cliffhanger.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:10:00.900
We bet that he's cooked up a solid and satisfying
ending to this unusually complex show.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:03.300
Ah, the mystery of Michael.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:08.100
The character is played to perfection by Ted
Danson, who manages to always be incredibly

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.940
charming and charismatic - even when he's
indulging his most diabolical impulses.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.780
"Okay, they're at each other's throats already…

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.490
This should put them over the top.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.430
Ed, you play Bart, a former private eye."

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:25.710
Even though Michael is a demon with access
to all the knowledge in the universe, audiences

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:27.660
still don't know a whole lot about him.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:32.120
He's made several references to his advanced
age and the fact that he's merely inhabiting

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.420
a human body... but how does that work, exactly?

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:40.240
Mike Schur has all but confirmed that audiences
will soon find out, telling Rolling Stone:

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:44.640
"You will learn a lot more about Michael’s
corporeal form in the fourth episode of this

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.140
season."

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:48.120
And that's not the only revelation they have
in store for us.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:52.720
As you've no doubt noticed, the concept of
"soulmates" runs through the entire show.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:59.320
"You'll all so beautiful tonight with your
regular-sized pockets and regular-sized soulmates."

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:03.930
Well, you can reportedly expect the idea of
"soulmates" to be further explored and developed

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:04.920
in the final season.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:10.540
In season two, fans only saw brief flashes
of the reboots Michael orchestrated in order

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.200
to trick Eleanor, Chidi, Tahani, and Jason.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:18.020
According to Mike Schur, some of these reboots
will be explored further in the final season.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.900
Speaking to Vanity Fair, he said,

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:23.680
"There's a lot of stuff that happens this
year where we sort of revisit the different

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:27.760
versions of Michael that have existed over
the time of the show, starting with the demon

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:31.600
version and going through the middle versions,
and going through the end versions."

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:36.360
And that brings us to the biggest question:
How will The Good Place ultimately conclude?

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:40.660
Kristen Bell seems to know something, but
she's keeping her cards close to her chest.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:44.980
Conan O'Brien asked whether she knows how
the show ends, and she responded:

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:46.200
"I forgot.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.080
I legit forgot."

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:48.420
"Did you really?"

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:48.920
"Yeah."

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.120
"So he told you where it's going and you forgot."

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:51.620
"Correct."

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:53.920
Well, we'll be getting some answers soon enough.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:59.100
Season four of The Good Place premieres on
Thursday, September 26th at 9 p.m. Eastern

00:11:59.100 --> 00:11:59.600
time.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:02.140
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:05.780
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
films are coming soon.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:09.680
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

